    "https://www.muskingum.edu/human-resources/careers": {
      "title": "Human Resources",
      "description": "Employment Opportunities | Muskingum University Skip to main navigation main menu Search Tools Canvas Campus Directory Employee Navigator MuskieLink Microsoft 365 Main menu About opener Mission & Values Quick Facts Our Alumni History Map & Directions Office of the President Admission & Aid opener Apply Visit Financial Aid Request Info Pay Deposit Transfer Students International Admission Login Academics opener Majors & Minors Disability Resource Services Registrar Academic Affairs eCampus Books Campus Life opener Academic Services Living on Campus Get Involved Recreation Safety & Wellness Student Life Campus Map Impact Center Graduate & Adult Learning opener Adult Degree Completion Master of Business Administration Master of Arts in Education Master of Arts in Teaching Health Related Programs Master of Occupational Therapy Master of Organizational Leadership Doctor of Organizational Leadership Accelerated Bachelor of Science in Nursing Online RN to BSN Nursing Master of Science in Nursing: Leadership & Education Secondary Menu Alumni Giving News Events Arts Athletics Library Directory Campus Map Gear Shop A-Z tools search Human Resources Home Human Resources Careers Careers Muskingum University values the exchange of diverse perspectives in its educational programs.  Muskingum actively seeks out and welcomes faculty, administrators, and staff who are committed to excellence in student learning and to full inclusivity at the university.  In addition, faculty should be committed to excellence in teaching, thrive in a collaborative environment of scholars, embrace experiential learning, and desire to mentor an inclusive student population. Administrative Careers Area Coordinator Counselor Digital Content Manager Director of Alumni and Parent Engagement Director of Graduate and Adult Learning Admission Director of Information Technology Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Athletic Careers Graduate Assistant - Archery (M&W) Faculty Careers No full-time vacancies at this time. All part-time teaching opportunities, including adjunct and clinical instructor (nursing) positions are available on an as-needed basis and are organized by department chairpersons; usually, they are not posted individually.  More information is available on the individual websites of the Academic Majors. Letters of interest, accompanied by a current CV, list of 3 professional references, and unofficial, graduate transcripts should be sent to careers@muskingum.edu , noting the department(s) to which you are applying within the subject line of the email. Support Staff Careers Building Technician Custodian Systems Mechanic and Maintenance Superviso r Student Employment Please review our Student Employment page to learn more about how to obtain your Certificate of Work Authorization, how to apply for a job, and how paychecks are deposited. Aramark Careers - Food and Auxiliary Services Please visit the Aramark website for more information about available positions. About Muskingum Founded in 1837, Muskingum University is a comprehensive university grounded in the liberal arts tradition and affiliated with the Presbyterian Church USA. Muskingum emphasizes entrepreneurial and experiential learning opportunities on its campus, in the community, and around the world. The University boasts an enrollment of 2,500 students in undergraduate, graduate and adult learning programs and offers more than sixty majors, four graduate degrees, and multiple degree completion and certificate opportunities. Muskingum currently offers 25 varsity sports , with 20 competing at the NCAA Division III level.  Muskingum competes in the Ohio Athletic Conference, which is the third oldest athletic conference in the United States. Muskingum University does not discriminate in its employment or educational programs or activities. If you need assistance or an accommodation due to a disability, please contact the Human Resources Office by emailing hr@muskingum.edu or by calling 740-826-8119. Human Resources Human Resources Careers Benefits opener Wellness Financial Retirement Leave Campus Amenities Downloadable Forms Policies Staff Council Student Employment Contact Back to top Main menu About opener Admission & Aid opener Academics opener Campus Life opener Graduate & Adult Learning opener 260 Stadium Drive New Concord, Ohio 43762-1837 (740) 826-8211 facebook twitter instagram youtube Footer Right Accreditations & Affiliations Human Resources Consumer Information Net Price Calculator Non-Discrimination Statement Website Feedback Title IX Veterans Facebook Pixel"
    },
    "https://www.muskingum.edu/human-resources/area-coordinator": {
      "title": "Area Coordinator",
      "description": "Area Coordinator | Muskingum University Skip to main navigation main menu Search Tools Canvas Campus Directory Employee Navigator MuskieLink Microsoft 365 Main menu About opener Mission & Values Quick Facts Our Alumni History Map & Directions Office of the President Admission & Aid opener Apply Visit Financial Aid Request Info Pay Deposit Transfer Students International Admission Login Academics opener Majors & Minors Disability Resource Services Registrar Academic Affairs eCampus Books Campus Life opener Academic Services Living on Campus Get Involved Recreation Safety & Wellness Student Life Campus Map Impact Center Graduate & Adult Learning opener Adult Degree Completion Master of Business Administration Master of Arts in Education Master of Arts in Teaching Health Related Programs Master of Occupational Therapy Master of Organizational Leadership Doctor of Organizational Leadership Accelerated Bachelor of Science in Nursing Online RN to BSN Nursing Master of Science in Nursing: Leadership & Education Secondary Menu Alumni Giving News Events Arts Athletics Library Directory Campus Map Gear Shop A-Z tools search Human Resources Home Human Resources Area Coordinator Area Coordinator Muskingum University has an immediate opening for an Area Coordinator.  This is an 11-month, full-time, live-in professional position responsible for managing on-campus residential facilities, residential life projects, and staffing.  In addition, this position provides targeted academic coaching, transition support, and student success programming, with particular emphasis on student-athletes and other students identified as needing additional support.  The Area Coordinator is an integral member of the Student Experience Division and collaborates across Student Life, Academic Services, and Athletics to support student success, persistence, and belonging. MAJOR RESPONSIBILITIES Manage a residential area of 100-200 residential students, including all of the responsibilities required therein. Communicate behavioral expectations and facilitate conflict resolution, roommate mediation, and respond to certain crisis situations. Establish a professional presence and facilitate positive community development in residential areas, know area residents and their issues/needs, and maintain availability in the residence halls and in the main Student Life Office. Coordinate delivery of developmental, educational, and social programming in residential areas. Supervise Resident Assistants in a manner that fosters development and responsibility. Serve on Student Life professional staff all campus on-call duty rotation and summer conference coordination team as necessary and respond to certain situations in person. Facilitate customer service delivery in Student Experience programs while balancing student wants and developmental needs. Provide individualized academic coaching and student success support for male student-athletes and other students identified through institutional referral processes, including assistance with time management, organization, study strategies, accountability, and connection to campus resources. Collaborate with Academic Affairs, Athletics, and other campus partners to identify students who may benefit from additional support and to coordinate appropriate academic and developmental interventions. Team teach or otherwise provide instructional support for designated student success courses, including Keys to Academic Success, with particular attention to students who may be less academically prepared for the transition to college. Develop and deliver group-based academic success programming for student-athletes and other targeted student populations, including workshops and programs focused on preparation for exams, effective study practices, academic routines, and end-of-semester success. Provide developmental support and mentoring to student-athletes as they navigate common transition and persistence challenges, including homesickness, team-role or playing-time frustrations, interpersonal concerns, and adjustment to college expectations; make referrals to appropriate professional resources when needs extend beyond the scope of the position. Build intentional relationships with student-athletes, coaches, faculty, and staff to strengthen student engagement, belonging, accountability, and persistence while maintaining appropriate professional boundaries and confidentiality. Represent the Student Experience Division on various committees, as assigned. Ability to perform evening and weekend work, and ability to meet regular and predictable attendance standards. The above statements reflect the general duties and responsibilities necessary to describe the major functions of the position and should not be considered a complete description of the essential functions of the position. This Job Description is not intended to be all inclusive.  The employee will be assigned by the immediate supervisor to perform other duties as needed or to perform other reasonably-related duties, including special projects. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Bachelor’s degree. Demonstrated ability to work in a collegial manner with co-workers and other constituencies. Strong verbal and written communication skills, as well as interpersonal skills. Demonstrated history of performing high-quality work with attention to detail. Ability to use general office equipment, programs, and software including office computer, Microsoft Office 365, copier, telephone, facsimile machine, etc. Ability to multi-task and engage in the gathering, examination, and basic analysis of information to determine solutions or recommendations and/or take appropriate action required. Demonstrated ability to build effective mentoring and coaching relationships with college students, particularly students who may benefit from additional academic or transition support. Knowledge of student success strategies, academic coaching practices, and appropriate referral to academic, counseling, wellness, and other campus resources. Ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, coaches, academic support professionals, and Student Affairs colleagues while maintaining appropriate confidentiality and professional boundaries. PREFERRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Master’s degree in Higher Education or related field. Understanding of a small, liberal arts, residential campus. Experience supporting student-athletes or working in a collegiate athletics environment. Experience with academic coaching, student success instruction, mentoring, or retention-focused programming. HOW TO APPLY Applications must include a statement of interest and current resume.  If not provided, references may be requested.  Application materials should be sent by email to careers@muskingum.edu or faxed to 740-826-6131.  Please include the position title in the subject line of your correspondence.  This position will remain open until filled, with review of applications to begin immediately. Muskingum University actively seeks out and welcomes administrators and staff who are committed to excellence in student learning, consider the engagement of diverse viewpoints in the University’s educational programs and activities, and are committed to full inclusivity at the University.  Muskingum University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes applications from all individuals. Muskingum University does not discriminate in its employment or educational programs or activities.  Please visit https://www.muskingum.edu/non-discrimination-statement to review the university’s official non-discrimination statement. Human Resources Human Resources Careers Benefits opener Wellness Financial Retirement Leave Campus Amenities Downloadable Forms Policies Staff Council Student Employment Contact Back to top Main menu About opener Admission & Aid opener Academics opener Campus Life opener Graduate & Adult Learning opener 260 Stadium Drive New Concord, Ohio 43762-1837 (740) 826-8211 facebook twitter instagram youtube Footer Right Accreditations & Affiliations Human Resources Consumer Information Net Price Calculator Non-Discrimination Statement Website Feedback Title IX Veterans Facebook Pixel"
    },
    "https://www.muskingum.edu/human-resources/digital-content-manager": {
      "title": "Digital Content Manager",
      "description": "Digital Content Manager | Muskingum University Skip to main navigation main menu Search Tools Canvas Campus Directory Employee Navigator MuskieLink Microsoft 365 Main menu About opener Mission & Values Quick Facts Our Alumni History Map & Directions Office of the President Admission & Aid opener Apply Visit Financial Aid Request Info Pay Deposit Transfer Students International Admission Login Academics opener Majors & Minors Disability Resource Services Registrar Academic Affairs eCampus Books Campus Life opener Academic Services Living on Campus Get Involved Recreation Safety & Wellness Student Life Campus Map Impact Center Graduate & Adult Learning opener Adult Degree Completion Master of Business Administration Master of Arts in Education Master of Arts in Teaching Health Related Programs Master of Occupational Therapy Master of Organizational Leadership Doctor of Organizational Leadership Accelerated Bachelor of Science in Nursing Online RN to BSN Nursing Master of Science in Nursing: Leadership & Education Secondary Menu Alumni Giving News Events Arts Athletics Library Directory Campus Map Gear Shop A-Z tools search Human Resources Home Human Resources Digital Content Manager Digital Content Manager Muskingum University invites applications for its Digital Content Manager. This position develops thoughtful, engaging, and vibrant content that tells the Muskingum story through its digital channels, with a primary focus on social media, photography, videography, and MAJOR RESPONSIBILITIES Develop creative, engaging, and audience-focused digital content consistent with institutional priorities and the Muskingum brand. Manage the University’s institutional social media channels, including content calendars, publishing, community engagement, and monitoring. Identify and develop digital storytelling opportunities highlighting students, faculty, alumni, academic programs, campus life, events, and accomplishments. Stay current on social media trends, platforms, algorithms, and best practices and adjust content strategy based on performance. Develop and implement paid and organic digital campaigns, including audience targeting, budgeting, optimization, and reporting. Monitor social media activity and escalate sensitive, reputational, privacy-related, or crisis-related issues as appropriate. Attend University events to capture and publish timely social media, photography, and video content. Serve as the University’s primary photographer, capturing and editing images for the website, social media, marketing collateral, advertising, and other institutional needs. Create and edit short-form video and multimedia content promoting the University, its programs, people, and events. Serve as the primary content manager for the University website, ensuring content is accurate, current, relevant, accessible, and consistent with University standards. Apply SEO, accessibility, and user experience best practices to website content and make recommendations to campus offices. Collaborate with the University’s web developer on website functionality, technical enhancements, integrations, and other back-end projects. Provide training and support for University employees who maintain web content and coordinate quarterly web captain meetings. Regularly consult with University departments and offices to identify content needs, provide guidance, and support their strategic goals, including student recruitment, enrollment, engagement, fundraising, institutional reputation, and community connection. Develop and maintain policies and best practices related to the University’s website, social media, photography, video, and digital content. Monitor website, social media, and campaign analytics and use data to improve digital content and strategy. Continually pursue new opportunities, platforms, and technologies to advance the University’s digital presence. The above statements reflect the general duties and responsibilities necessary to describe the major functions of the position and should not be considered a complete description of the essential functions of the position.  It is not intended to be inclusive, and the employee will be perform other reasonable related duties as assigned by the immediate supervisor. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Bachelor’s degree, preferably in communications, marketing, journalism, digital media, or related field of study. Minimum of three years of professional experience in digital communications, social media, website content management, photography, videography, or related field. Strong knowledge of social media platforms, audiences, trends, algorithms, analytics, and best practices. Strong writing, editing, proofreading, and digital storytelling skills. Demonstrated photography skills, including event, portrait, and candid photography. Experience creating and editing short-form video and multimedia content. Proficiency with Adobe Creative Cloud or comparable photography, video, and audio editing tools. Experience creating and maintaining website content in Drupal or a similar content management system. Basic understanding of HTML and CSS for content formatting and troubleshooting. Experience with SEO, web accessibility, and web and social media analytics. Sound editorial judgment and ability to recognize issues requiring consultation or escalation. Excellent project management, organizational, communication, and collaboration skills. Ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines while maintaining accuracy, quality, and brand consistency. Ability to work occasional nights and weekends to photograph, record, and provide social media coverage of University events. PREFERRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Experience developing and managing paid digital or social media campaigns preferred. Understanding of copyright, privacy, FERPA, and accessibility in digital content creation. Experience managing higher education social media channels using tools such as Buffer. HOW TO APPLY Applications must include a statement of interest and current resume.  If not provided, references may be requested.  Application materials should be sent by email to careers@muskingum.edu or faxed to 740-826-6131.  Please include the position title in the subject line of your correspondence.  This position will remain open until filled, with review of applications to begin immediately. Muskingum University actively seeks out and welcomes administrators and staff who are committed to excellence in student learning, consider the engagement of diverse viewpoints in the University’s educational programs and activities, and are committed to full inclusivity at the University.  Muskingum University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes applications from all individuals. Muskingum University does not discriminate in its employment or educational programs or activities.  Please visit https://www.muskingum.edu/non-discrimination-statement to review the university’s official non-discrimination statement. Human Resources Human Resources Careers Benefits opener Wellness Financial Retirement Leave Campus Amenities Downloadable Forms Policies Staff Council Student Employment Contact Back to top Main menu About opener Admission & Aid opener Academics opener Campus Life opener Graduate & Adult Learning opener 260 Stadium Drive New Concord, Ohio 43762-1837 (740) 826-8211 facebook twitter instagram youtube Footer Right Accreditations & Affiliations Human Resources Consumer Information Net Price Calculator Non-Discrimination Statement Website Feedback Title IX Veterans Facebook Pixel"
    },
    "https://www.muskingum.edu/human-resources/director-alumni-and-parent-engagement": {
      "title": "Director of Alumni and Parent Engagement",
      "description": "Director of Alumni and Parent Engagement | Muskingum University Skip to main navigation main menu Search Tools Canvas Campus Directory Employee Navigator MuskieLink Microsoft 365 Main menu About opener Mission & Values Quick Facts Our Alumni History Map & Directions Office of the President Admission & Aid opener Apply Visit Financial Aid Request Info Pay Deposit Transfer Students International Admission Login Academics opener Majors & Minors Disability Resource Services Registrar Academic Affairs eCampus Books Campus Life opener Academic Services Living on Campus Get Involved Recreation Safety & Wellness Student Life Campus Map Impact Center Graduate & Adult Learning opener Adult Degree Completion Master of Business Administration Master of Arts in Education Master of Arts in Teaching Health Related Programs Master of Occupational Therapy Master of Organizational Leadership Doctor of Organizational Leadership Accelerated Bachelor of Science in Nursing Online RN to BSN Nursing Master of Science in Nursing: Leadership & Education Secondary Menu Alumni Giving News Events Arts Athletics Library Directory Campus Map Gear Shop A-Z tools search Human Resources Home Human Resources Director of Alumni and Parent Engagement Director of Alumni and Parent Engagement Muskingum University invites applications for its Director of Alumni and Parent Engagement.  Alumni and parents of students are the foremost brand ambassadors for the university, and their advocacy, involvement and philanthropic support are essential components for a thriving institution. The Director will provide strategic leadership in developing a long-term vision and will develop and execute the strategies, programming, and activities for robust alumni and parent engagement. MAJOR RESPONSIBILITIES Alumni Engagement and Events Develop a long-term vision for alumni and parent engagement, including: The development and maintenance of key performance metrics, such as engagement rate, donor participation, event cost per attendee and event conversions, volunteer participation rate, prospects identified through engagement, email and online engagement. The development and implementation of an annual plan that includes strategies, goals, an action plan for meeting the goals, and an operating budget for engagement, Strategies may encompass a broad range of channels including in-person and virtual channels for engagement, provided they support meeting established goals. Collaboration with the Vice President for Institutional Advancement to establish annual goals for each metric that will gauge success in meeting program goals and approval of plans and budgets. Lead and administer an effective alumni awards strategy/program, including but not limited to Distinguished Service and Emerging Alumni Awards. Seek ways for ongoing engagement with awardees, past and present. Coordinate with the Director of Donor Relations in establishing and administering a University Lifetime Philanthropy Award and Leadership Award. Assist in developing alignment between alumni awards and philanthropic goals. Provide leadership to and support the activities of the University’s Alumni Council. Work with the Vice President and Philanthropy Officers to engage alumni and friends in targeted geographic areas through special events, virtual engagement opportunities, and other high-value programming that foster opportunities for annual support and potentially, the engagement of major gift prospects. Develop and implement a sustainable process to recruit, train, and support alumni volunteers to achieve program goals and objectives. Coordinate with the IMPACT Center to implement a quality mentorship program that connects alumni with current students to provide meaningful engagement opportunities. Support efforts of the Director of Annual Giving to engage alumni through annual and special opportunities for giving. Work with the Marketing and Communications Office to ensure a dynamic alumni presence in the University’s marketing/communication efforts on the website and in designated print, electronic, and social media platforms. Oversee the University’s alumni social media pages on Facebook and Instagram and other sites as an opportunity to shape alumni perception of Muskingum University. CRM Optimization Support ongoing performance improvement of the Advancement Slate CRM by participating in professional development. Collaborate with Advancement Services and MU’s Slate Specialist as needed to problem solve, and support implementation of system refinements to all Advancement units. The above statements reflect the general duties and responsibilities necessary to describe the major functions of the position and should not be considered a complete description of the essential functions of the position. It is not intended to be all inclusive, and the employee will perform other reasonable related duties as assigned by the immediate supervisor. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Bachelor’s degree At least 3 years of job-related experience Availability work evenings and weekends and to travel overnight on a limited basis for events Excellent written and verbal communication skills Excellent project management, organizational, and planning skills Strong interpersonal skills to relate with alumni across generations, in-person, by phone, and virtually Ability to interface cross-functionally across departments and to collaborate effectively with a team Willingness to innovate and create solutions for ongoing challenges Self-starter with initiative and follow through High-level attention to detail, consistency, and accuracy Ability to work both collaboratively and independently Strong technology skills including social media, CRM experience, and all Microsoft 365 applications Ability to gather, examine, and analyze information to either solve problems or make recommendations to the VPIA and/or take appropriate action as required Ability to maintain confidentiality regarding constituent information HOW TO APPLY Applications must include a statement of interest and current resume.  If not provided, references may be requested.  Application materials should be sent by email to careers@muskingum.edu or faxed to 740-826-6131.  Please include the position title in the subject line of your correspondence.  This position will remain open until filled, with review of applications to begin on August 10, 2026. Muskingum University actively seeks out and welcomes administrators and staff who are committed to excellence in student learning, consider the engagement of diverse viewpoints in the University’s educational programs and activities, and are committed to full inclusivity at the University.  Muskingum University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes applications from all individuals. Muskingum University does not discriminate in its employment or educational programs or activities.  Please visit https://www.muskingum.edu/non-discrimination-statement to review the university’s official non-discrimination statement. Human Resources Human Resources Careers Benefits opener Wellness Financial Retirement Leave Campus Amenities Downloadable Forms Policies Staff Council Student Employment Contact Back to top Main menu About opener Admission & Aid opener Academics opener Campus Life opener Graduate & Adult Learning opener 260 Stadium Drive New Concord, Ohio 43762-1837 (740) 826-8211 facebook twitter instagram youtube Footer Right Accreditations & Affiliations Human Resources Consumer Information Net Price Calculator Non-Discrimination Statement Website Feedback Title IX Veterans Facebook Pixel"
    },
    "https://www.muskingum.edu/human-resources/director-graduate-and-adult-learning-admission": {
      "title": "Director of Graduate and Adult Learning Admission",
      "description": "Director of Graduate and Adult Learning Admission | Muskingum University Skip to main navigation main menu Search Tools Canvas Campus Directory Employee Navigator MuskieLink Microsoft 365 Main menu About opener Mission & Values Quick Facts Our Alumni History Map & Directions Office of the President Admission & Aid opener Apply Visit Financial Aid Request Info Pay Deposit Transfer Students International Admission Login Academics opener Majors & Minors Disability Resource Services Registrar Academic Affairs eCampus Books Campus Life opener Academic Services Living on Campus Get Involved Recreation Safety & Wellness Student Life Campus Map Impact Center Graduate & Adult Learning opener Adult Degree Completion Master of Business Administration Master of Arts in Education Master of Arts in Teaching Health Related Programs Master of Occupational Therapy Master of Organizational Leadership Doctor of Organizational Leadership Accelerated Bachelor of Science in Nursing Online RN to BSN Nursing Master of Science in Nursing: Leadership & Education Secondary Menu Alumni Giving News Events Arts Athletics Library Directory Campus Map Gear Shop A-Z tools search Human Resources Home Human Resources Director of Graduate and Adult Learning Admission Director of Graduate and Adult Learning Admission Muskingum University invites applications for the Director of Graduate and Adult Learning (GAL) Admission.  Reporting to the Vice President for Enrollment and Marketing (VPEM), the Director will provide strategic leadership and accountability for graduate and adult recruitment, including the development, execution, and continuous improvement of enrollment strategy and outcomes. MAJOR RESPONSIBILITIES Collaborate closely with the VPEM, along with the Provost and the GAL Program Directors, to establish and achieve enrollment goals for graduate and adult learners. Analyze enrollment data across programs to identify trends, monitor performance, and inform strategic adjustments. Build strong partnerships with academic departments and programs, the Office of External Engagement, the Student Experience Division, and other university stakeholders to support GAL recruitment. Guide development of communication and outreach strategies for prospective GAL students in collaboration with the Admission Operations team, Academic Affairs, and Strategic Marketing & Communication. Lead implementation and optimization of technology platforms - including CRM tools - to support efficient and effective messaging across GAL populations. Evaluate and manage partnerships with third-party vendors supporting recruitment, lead generation and enrollment marketing. Represent the university at key events and within professional networks to stay informed of trends and best practices in GAL enrollment. Responsible for budget duties as assigned. Conduct market analysis to identify emerging opportunities and new student populations for graduate and adult learning programs. The above statements reflect the general duties and responsibilities necessary to describe the major functions of the position and should not be considered a complete description of the essential functions of the position.  This Job Description is not intended to be all inclusive.  The employee will be assigned by the immediate supervisor to perform other duties as needed or to perform other reasonable related duties, including special projects. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Bachelor’s degree, with at least 5 years of progressive leadership experience in higher education enrollment management; master’s degree preferred. Significant experience in graduate and/or adult recruitment and enrollment strategy. Strong staff management, mentoring, and team-building abilities. Excellent communication and relationship-building skills across a variety of stakeholders. Familiarity with CRM systems (e.g., Slate) and data-informed decision-making in recruitment and operations. HOW TO APPLY Applications must include a statement of interest and current resume.  If not provided, references may be requested.  Application materials should be sent by email to careers@muskingum.edu or faxed to 740-826-6131.  Please include the position title in the subject line of your correspondence.  This position will remain posted until filled, with review of applications to begin on August 17, 2026. Muskingum University actively seeks out and welcomes administrators and staff who are committed to excellence in student learning, consider the engagement of diverse viewpoints in the University’s educational programs and activities, and are committed to full inclusivity at the University.  Muskingum University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes applications from all individuals. Muskingum University does not discriminate in its employment or educational programs or activities.  Please visit https://www.muskingum.edu/non-discrimination-statement to review the university’s official non-discrimination statement. Human Resources Human Resources Careers Benefits opener Wellness Financial Retirement Leave Campus Amenities Downloadable Forms Policies Staff Council Student Employment Contact Back to top Main menu About opener Admission & Aid opener Academics opener Campus Life opener Graduate & Adult Learning opener 260 Stadium Drive New Concord, Ohio 43762-1837 (740) 826-8211 facebook twitter instagram youtube Footer Right Accreditations & Affiliations Human Resources Consumer Information Net Price Calculator Non-Discrimination Statement Website Feedback Title IX Veterans Facebook Pixel"
    },
    "https://www.muskingum.edu/human-resources/director-information-technology": {
      "title": "Director of Information Technology",
      "description": "Director of Information Technology | Muskingum University Skip to main navigation main menu Search Tools Canvas Campus Directory Employee Navigator MuskieLink Microsoft 365 Main menu About opener Mission & Values Quick Facts Our Alumni History Map & Directions Office of the President Admission & Aid opener Apply Visit Financial Aid Request Info Pay Deposit Transfer Students International Admission Login Academics opener Majors & Minors Disability Resource Services Registrar Academic Affairs eCampus Books Campus Life opener Academic Services Living on Campus Get Involved Recreation Safety & Wellness Student Life Campus Map Impact Center Graduate & Adult Learning opener Adult Degree Completion Master of Business Administration Master of Arts in Education Master of Arts in Teaching Health Related Programs Master of Occupational Therapy Master of Organizational Leadership Doctor of Organizational Leadership Accelerated Bachelor of Science in Nursing Online RN to BSN Nursing Master of Science in Nursing: Leadership & Education Secondary Menu Alumni Giving News Events Arts Athletics Library Directory Campus Map Gear Shop A-Z tools search Human Resources Home Human Resources Director of Information Technology Director of Information Technology Muskingum University invites applications for its Director of Information Technology.  This position will take a hands-on, collaborative approach to leading the University's technology operations and helping shape a practical, service-oriented technology strategy. This is a working leadership role for an experienced technology professional who can balance strategic planning with day-to-day operational oversight, guide a small IT team, partner effectively with campus stakeholders, and coordinate specialized external providers where appropriate. Reporting to the Vice President for Finance & Operations, the Director will provide leadership across enterprise applications, infrastructure, cybersecurity, service management, vendor relationships, business continuity, and technology planning. The successful candidate will help preserve institutional knowledge, strengthen documentation and operating procedures, improve the consistency of IT support, and establish a sustainable model for serving the University's academic, administrative, residential, and digital-campus needs. Muskingum offers a full benefits package, which includes, but is not limited to, a generous paid-time off package and immediate access to tuition remission or exchange for employees who are eligible.  More information about benefits is available at: https://www.muskingum.edu/human-resources/benefits . This position is not eligible for sponsorship. STRATEGIC PRIORITIES FOR THE DIRECTOR OF INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY The Director of Information Technology will help strengthen the University's technology capabilities by focusing on several key priorities: Providing Hands-On Technology Leadership. Lead a small IT organization with a practical player-coach approach, combining sound strategic judgment with visible engagement in day-to-day operations and problem solving. Strengthening Service Delivery. Improve help desk operations, request prioritization, escalation practices, knowledge management, service ownership, metrics, and continuous improvement using the University's service-management platform. Preserving Knowledge and Operational Continuity. Build documentation, cross-training, succession coverage, and repeatable procedures so that essential services do not depend on the undocumented knowledge of a small number of individuals. Advancing Cybersecurity and Resilience. Guide a risk-based cybersecurity program, coordinate assessment follow-up, strengthen incident readiness, and improve business-continuity and disaster-recovery planning. Supporting Core Administrative and Academic Systems. Provide effective oversight for the University's enterprise applications, integrations, data, identity services, productivity tools, classroom technology, and digital-campus needs. Building a Sustainable Support Model. Clarify internal responsibilities, develop staff capability, and establish a right-sized approach to vendor and managed-service-provider support while retaining appropriate institutional ownership. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Leadership, Strategy, and Campus Partnership Develop and maintain a practical technology roadmap aligned with the University's mission, priorities, resources, and risk profile. Serve as a trusted technology partner to University leadership, academic and administrative departments, and campus stakeholders. Translate technology issues into clear business terms and provide well-reasoned recommendations for priorities, investments, and tradeoffs. Promote a collaborative, respectful, and service-oriented IT culture that supports both technical and nontechnical users. IT Operations, Service Management, and Continuity Oversee day-to-day IT operations, including help desk services, ticket intake, prioritization, escalation, service ownership, user communication, and issue follow-through. Strengthen the practical use of TeamDynamix for ticketing, asset management, reporting, knowledge management, and continuous improvement. Establish clear operating procedures, documentation standards, support coverage plans, and after-hours escalation practices. Guide business-continuity, backup, recovery, and disaster-recovery planning and ensure that recovery procedures are documented and periodically tested. Enterprise Applications, Data, and Digital Campus Services Provide oversight for the University's enterprise application portfolio, including Ellucian Colleague, Microsoft 365, related integrations, and other administrative and academic systems. Work closely with functional and technical staff to support the reliability, security, documentation, and effective use of the University's ERP/SIS environment. Support sound practices for identity and access management, data governance, institutional reporting, application ownership, and lifecycle planning. Help ensure that technology services effectively support classroom instruction, online and hybrid learning, adult and graduate programs, and off-campus users. Cybersecurity, Risk, and Compliance Lead a risk-based cybersecurity program appropriate to the University's size, mission, and regulatory obligations. Coordinate cybersecurity assessments, remediation planning, insurance requirements, policies, access controls, security awareness, and incident-response readiness. Work with internal staff and specialized providers to monitor risk, prioritize improvements, and maintain clear accountability for security-related activities. Promote practical use of recognized cybersecurity frameworks, including NIST-based assessment and improvement practices. Infrastructure, Projects, and Vendor Management Provide leadership oversight for network services, servers, storage, backup, endpoints, telecommunications, classroom technology, and residential connectivity. Guide major technology initiatives, including infrastructure improvements, service-provider transitions, and communications-modernization efforts. Maintain appropriate lifecycle planning for technology assets and incorporate replacement needs into annual planning and budgeting. Manage technology vendors, contracts, service levels, support relationships, and escalation paths; evaluate where internal, outsourced, or co-managed support models are most appropriate. Team Leadership and Development Lead, coach, and develop a small IT team with clear roles, priorities, accountability, and opportunities for professional growth. Establish cross-training and knowledge-transfer practices that reduce single-person dependency and improve operational resilience. Identify staffing, skill, and support gaps and recommend practical solutions that may include internal development, hiring, process improvement, or external support. RELATIONSHIP WITH THE UNIVERSITY COMMUNITY The Director of Information Technology will work closely with University leadership, academic and administrative departments, faculty, staff, students, IT team members, and external service providers. The Director will be expected to listen carefully, communicate clearly, establish priorities transparently, and build effective partnerships across the University. The role requires a leader who is comfortable moving between strategic conversations, operational planning, and hands-on problem solving when needed. THE FIRST 12 MONTHS The Director of Information Technology will be expected to establish a strong foundation for sustainable technology operations during the first year. Likely priorities include: Complete Knowledge Transition and Stabilization. Capture essential operating knowledge, clarify immediate coverage needs, and establish continuity for critical systems, configurations, vendor relationships, and support processes. Create an IT Service-Delivery Baseline. Review help desk operations, use TeamDynamix consistently, define escalation practices, and establish practical service metrics and reporting. Establish a Cybersecurity Improvement Roadmap. Review available assessment findings, confirm priority risks, strengthen incident readiness, and develop a realistic remediation plan. Clarify the IT Operating Model. Evaluate staffing, role clarity, cross-training needs, and the appropriate use of co-managed or outsourced support for selected services. Develop a Technology Roadmap and Lifecycle Plan. Document priorities for infrastructure, applications, classroom technology, communications, digital-campus services, asset replacement, and annual investment planning. Guide Active Technology Transitions. Provide leadership for current network, telecommunications, and service-provider transition activities while strengthening documentation and accountability. The above statements reflect the general duties and responsibilities necessary to describe the major functions of the position and should not be considered a complete description of the essential functions of the position. This Job Description is not intended to be all inclusive.  The employee will be assigned by the immediate supervisor to perform other duties as needed or to perform other reasonable related duties, including special projects. HOW TO APPLY Applications must include a cover letter describing the candidate’s experience in relation to the stated job responsibilities, a resume, and a list of 3 professional references and should be sent to careers@muskingum.edu .  Please include the position title in the subject line of your email.  This position will remain open until filled, with priority consideration given to applicants who apply by August 11, 2026. Muskingum University actively seeks out and welcomes administrators and staff who are committed to excellence in student learning, consider the engagement of diverse viewpoints in the University’s educational programs and activities, and are committed to full inclusivity at the University.  Muskingum University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes applications from all individuals. Muskingum University does not discriminate in its employment or educational programs or activities.  Please visit https://www.muskingum.edu/non-discrimination-statement to review the university’s official non-discrimination statement. Human Resources Human Resources Careers Benefits opener Wellness Financial Retirement Leave Campus Amenities Downloadable Forms Policies Staff Council Student Employment Contact Back to top Main menu About opener Admission & Aid opener Academics opener Campus Life opener Graduate & Adult Learning opener 260 Stadium Drive New Concord, Ohio 43762-1837 (740) 826-8211 facebook twitter instagram youtube Footer Right Accreditations & Affiliations Human Resources Consumer Information Net Price Calculator Non-Discrimination Statement Website Feedback Title IX Veterans Facebook Pixel"
    },
    "https://www.muskingum.edu/human-resources/executive-director-marketing-and-communications": {
      "title": "Executive Director of Marketing and Communications",
      "description": "Executive Director of Marketing and Communications | Muskingum University Skip to main navigation main menu Search Tools Canvas Campus Directory Employee Navigator MuskieLink Microsoft 365 Main menu About opener Mission & Values Quick Facts Our Alumni History Map & Directions Office of the President Admission & Aid opener Apply Visit Financial Aid Request Info Pay Deposit Transfer Students International Admission Login Academics opener Majors & Minors Disability Resource Services Registrar Academic Affairs eCampus Books Campus Life opener Academic Services Living on Campus Get Involved Recreation Safety & Wellness Student Life Campus Map Impact Center Graduate & Adult Learning opener Adult Degree Completion Master of Business Administration Master of Arts in Education Master of Arts in Teaching Health Related Programs Master of Occupational Therapy Master of Organizational Leadership Doctor of Organizational Leadership Accelerated Bachelor of Science in Nursing Online RN to BSN Nursing Master of Science in Nursing: Leadership & Education Secondary Menu Alumni Giving News Events Arts Athletics Library Directory Campus Map Gear Shop A-Z tools search Human Resources Home Human Resources Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Muskingum University invites applications for the position of Executive Director of Marketing and Communications.  The successful candidate will be a results-oriented and collaborative leader, responsible for executing integrated marketing and communications initiatives that support enrollment growth, institutional visibility, and stakeholder engagement. Leading the day-to-day operations of marketing and communications, this position translates institutional strategy into high-impact marketing campaigns and communications. MAJOR RESPONSIBILITIES Campaign Execution & Marketing Operations Lead the planning, execution, and delivery of integrated marketing campaigns aligned with institutional enrollment and branding goals. Implement recruitment, engagement, and awareness campaigns across multiple channels, including digital, print, email, and social media. Manage marketing calendars, timelines, and workflows to ensure timely and effective delivery of projects. Lead the transition from a request-based service model to campaign-based planning, including standardized project intake, prioritization tied to enrollment goals, and defined service-level expectations for campus partners. Enrollment Marketing Support Partner closely with Admission and Student Financial Services to develop and implement recruitment and yield campaigns. Support segmentation and personalization strategies defined by senior leadership. Scale digital lead generation, search engine optimization, and conversion-focused campaigns supporting undergraduate, graduate, and adult learning enrollment growth. Ensure that messaging developed by the marketing team is consistently reflected in CRM communication flows, including inquiry follow-up and yield communications. Content, Creative & Brand Implementation Oversee development of creative assets, ensuring consistency with institutional brand standards and messaging. Supervise content creation across platforms (web, print, digital, social), ensuring quality, clarity, and audience alignment. Maintain brand integrity through consistent application of visual identity, tone, and messaging. Establish shared content ownership with academic programs, Advancement, and other campus partners by refining, packaging, and amplifying content provided by campus partners. Prioritize outcome-focused storytelling, including alumni success, career outcomes, and employer partnership stories, in collaboration with Advancement and the Impact Center. Digital Marketing & Channel Management Manage the University’s digital presence, including website content, social media channels, email marketing, and digital advertising campaigns. Coordinate updates, enhancements, and user experience improvements for digital properties. Project Management & Team Leadership Supervise marketing and communications staff, including creative and digital team members. Establish clear workflows, priorities, and accountability for project delivery. Manage relationships with external vendors, agencies, and freelancers as needed. Ensure efficient use of resources and adherence to budgets. Partner with the department’s Project Manager on intake coordination, timeline development, and workflow tracking. Data, Analytics & Performance Tracking Monitor campaign performance metrics (e.g., inquiries, engagement, conversion rates) and report outcomes to the Vice President. Use data insights to refine and improve ongoing campaigns and tactics. Support tracking of ROI for marketing activities and contribute to continuous improvement efforts. Communications & Coordination Oversee institutional communications, including announcements, publications, and key messaging initiatives. Support media relations efforts and assist with communication needs as directed. Serve as a key liaison with campus partners to manage project requests and ensure alignment with institutional priorities. The above statements reflect the general duties and responsibilities necessary to describe the major functions of the position and should not be considered a complete description of the essential functions of the position. This Job Description is not intended to be all inclusive.  The employee will be assigned by the immediate supervisor to perform other duties as needed or to perform other related duties, including special projects. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Bachelor’s degree in marketing, communications, or related field (Master’s preferred). 5+ years of progressive experience in marketing, communications, or related roles. Demonstrated success in executing integrated marketing campaigns and managing multiple projects simultaneously. Strong understanding of digital marketing tools, platforms, and best practices. Excellent organizational, communication, and project management skills. Experience supervising staff or leading project teams. Strong attention to detail and execution. Demonstrated success in project and workflow management. Ability to make data-informed decisions to optimize the work of the office. Strong collaborative and relationship-building skills. Demonstrated responsiveness and ability to adapt. Demonstrated effectiveness in brand stewardship. HOW TO APPLY Applications must include a cover letter describing the candidate’s experience in relation to the stated job responsibilities, a resume, and a list of 3 professional references and should be sent to careers@muskingum.edu .  Please include the position title in the subject line of your email.  This position will remain open until filled, with review of candidates to begin immediately. Muskingum University actively seeks out and welcomes administrators and staff who are committed to excellence in student learning, consider the engagement of diverse viewpoints in the University’s educational programs and activities, and are committed to full inclusivity at the University.  Muskingum University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes applications from all individuals. Muskingum University does not discriminate in its employment or educational programs or activities.  Please visit https://www.muskingum.edu/non-discrimination-statement to review the university’s official non-discrimination statement. Human Resources Human Resources Careers Benefits opener Wellness Financial Retirement Leave Campus Amenities Downloadable Forms Policies Staff Council Student Employment Contact Back to top Main menu About opener Admission & Aid opener Academics opener Campus Life opener Graduate & Adult Learning opener 260 Stadium Drive New Concord, Ohio 43762-1837 (740) 826-8211 facebook twitter instagram youtube Footer Right Accreditations & Affiliations Human Resources Consumer Information Net Price Calculator Non-Discrimination Statement Website Feedback Title IX Veterans Facebook Pixel"
    },
    "https://www.muskingum.edu/human-resources/graduate-assistant-archery-mw": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant - Archery (M&W) | Muskingum University Skip to main navigation main menu Search Tools Canvas Campus Directory Employee Navigator MuskieLink Microsoft 365 Main menu About opener Mission & Values Quick Facts Our Alumni History Map & Directions Office of the President Admission & Aid opener Apply Visit Financial Aid Request Info Pay Deposit Transfer Students International Admission Login Academics opener Majors & Minors Disability Resource Services Registrar Academic Affairs eCampus Books Campus Life opener Academic Services Living on Campus Get Involved Recreation Safety & Wellness Student Life Campus Map Impact Center Graduate & Adult Learning opener Adult Degree Completion Master of Business Administration Master of Arts in Education Master of Arts in Teaching Health Related Programs Master of Occupational Therapy Master of Organizational Leadership Doctor of Organizational Leadership Accelerated Bachelor of Science in Nursing Online RN to BSN Nursing Master of Science in Nursing: Leadership & Education Secondary Menu Alumni Giving News Events Arts Athletics Library Directory Campus Map Gear Shop A-Z tools search Human Resources Home Human Resources Graduate Assistant - Archery (M&W) Graduate Assistant - Archery (M&W) Muskingum University invites applications for a Graduate Assistant for the men's and women's Archery teams. This position is responsible for assisting in the overall coaching and management of the Archery teams, at the direction of the Head Coach. MAJOR RESPONSIBILITIES Participate in all aspects of recruiting prospective student-athletes, including mailings, Front Rush, texts/calls, off campus evaluations, and campus visits Assist with all practice planning and execution Assist the head coach in competition and travel preparations Assist the head coach with assigned administrative duties, such as event scheduling, budget management, procurement of equipment, and fundraising Assist with conducting pre-season, in-season, and post-season conditioning/lifting, within the guidelines and bylaws of USA Archery May be assigned limited teaching opportunities The above statements reflect the general duties and responsibilities necessary to describe the major functions of the position and should not be considered a complete description of the essential functions of the position.  This Job Description is not intended to be all inclusive.  The employee will be assigned by the immediate supervisor to perform other duties as needed or to perform other reasonably related duties, including special projects. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Undergraduate degree. Acceptance or ability to be accepted into Muskingum University Graduate Program. Strong collegiate background in Archery. Ability to collaborate and participate as an active member of the athletic department and the University community Good organizational and leadership skills. Excellent verbal and written communication skills, as well as interpersonal skills. HOW TO APPLY Applications must include a statement of interest and current resume.  If not provided, references may be requested.  Application materials should be sent by email to careers@muskingum.edu or faxed to 740-826-6131.  Please include the position title in the subject line of your correspondence.  This position will remain open until filled, with review of applications to begin immediately. Muskingum University actively seeks out and welcomes administrators and staff who are committed to excellence in student learning, consider the engagement of diverse viewpoints in the University’s educational programs and activities, and are committed to full inclusivity at the University.  Muskingum University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes applications from all individuals. Muskingum University does not discriminate in its employment or educational programs or activities.  Please visit https://www.muskingum.edu/non-discrimination-statement to review the university’s official non-discrimination statement. Human Resources Human Resources Careers Benefits opener Wellness Financial Retirement Leave Campus Amenities Downloadable Forms Policies Staff Council Student Employment Contact Back to top Main menu About opener Admission & Aid opener Academics opener Campus Life opener Graduate & Adult Learning opener 260 Stadium Drive New Concord, Ohio 43762-1837 (740) 826-8211 facebook twitter instagram youtube Footer Right Accreditations & Affiliations Human Resources Consumer Information Net Price Calculator Non-Discrimination Statement Website Feedback Title IX Veterans Facebook Pixel"
