    "https://www.muskingum.edu/human-resources/building-technician": {
      "title": "Building Technician",
      "description": "Building Technician | Muskingum University Skip to main navigation main menu Search Tools Canvas Campus Directory Employee Navigator MuskieLink Microsoft 365 Main menu About opener Mission & Values Quick Facts Our Alumni History Map & Directions Office of the President Admission & Aid opener Apply Visit Financial Aid Request Info Pay Deposit Transfer Students International Admission Login Academics opener Majors & Minors Disability Resource Services Registrar Academic Affairs eCampus Books Campus Life opener Academic Services Living on Campus Get Involved Recreation Safety & Wellness Student Life Campus Map Impact Center Graduate & Adult Learning opener Adult Degree Completion Master of Business Administration Master of Arts in Education Master of Arts in Teaching Health Related Programs Master of Occupational Therapy Master of Organizational Leadership Doctor of Organizational Leadership Accelerated Bachelor of Science in Nursing Online RN to BSN Nursing Master of Science in Nursing: Leadership & Education Secondary Menu Alumni Giving News Events Arts Athletics Library Directory Campus Map Gear Shop A-Z tools search Human Resources Home Human Resources Building Technician Building Technician Muskingum University invites applications for a Building Technician. This position handles more complex facilities maintenance, troubleshooting, and overseeing the operation of advanced systems, including HVAC, electrical, plumbing, and specialized equipment. This role requires a higher level of responsibility in infrastructure oversight. Muskingum offers a full benefits package, which includes, but is not limited to, a generous paid-time off package and immediate access to tuition remission or exchange for employees who are eligible. More information about benefits is available at: https://www.muskingum.edu/human-resources/benefits . MAJOR RESPONSIBILITIES Dust mop, sweep, wet mop, and spray-buff floors. Vacuum and clean rugs and carpets. Scrub floors with machines. Scrub and clean restroom fixtures; keep restrooms supplied with towels, soap and other appropriate items. Dust and clean walls, doors, windows, woodwork, and other above-floor surfaces. Clean elevators, stairwells, and outside entrances. Keep records and make reports as instructed by Custodial Team Leader. Notify Custodial Team Leader of equipment and facilities needing repair or replacement. Replace accessible light bulbs. Collect and dispose of trash. Lock and unlock buildings and doors as directed. Communicate to Team Leader any potential safety or mechanical hazards observed. Maintain supply closet and inventory. Supervise student helpers as assigned.  Assign tasks, monitor work, provide feedback and evaluate work. Vacuum furniture and drapes. Wash waste receptacles. Shovel and remove snow. Event set-ups as required, assist in moving tents, stage, tables, chairs, etc... Strip and refinish floors. Wash walls, vents and radiators. Wash and vacuum light fixtures. Shampoo carpets. The above statements reflect the general duties and responsibilities necessary to describe the major functions of the position and should not be considered a complete description of the essential functions of the position.  This Job Description is not intended to be all inclusive.  The employee will be assigned by the immediate supervisor to perform other duties as needed or to perform other reasonably related duties, including special projects. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Troubleshoot and maintain HVAC systems, controls, alarm systems, boilers, refrigeration, and electrical interfaces. Conduct inspections, troubleshooting, and necessary maintenance to ensure a safe and comfortable working environment. Retrofit and service new systems, as well as diagnose, repair, and maintain building automation systems. Assist with the oversight and maintenance of infrastructure, including plumbing, electrical, steam, hot water systems, lighting, and sound systems. Evaluate the need for external contract services and oversee their usage. Collaborate with others in the department for specialized repair and maintenance projects. Comply with service standards, work instructions, and customer requirements. Keep up to date on work order requests, maintain logs and records, and ensure proper closure of work order requests. Maintain purchasing receipts and proper documentation for work order completion. Ability to climb ladders, enter tight spaces, work in tunnels, and other mechanical spaces. Must be able to respond 24/7 for trouble call backs. The above statements reflect the general duties and responsibilities necessary to describe the major functions of the position and should not be considered a complete description of the essential functions of the position. This Job Description is not intended to be all inclusive. The employee will be assigned by the immediate supervisor to perform other duties as needed or to perform other reasonably related duties, including special projects. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Advanced knowledge and competency in HVAC systems and controls. Universal refrigerant recovery license and proficiency in handling refrigerants. Working knowledge of telecommunication systems. Ability to understand system interdependencies and how issues may impact other systems. Proficient in using computers and relevant software for troubleshooting and maintenance. Ability to cross-train to learn to repair and maintain plumbing, electrical, and restaurant equipment. HOW TO APPLY Applications must include a statement of interest and current resume. If not provided, references may be requested.  Application materials should be sent by email to careers@muskingum.edu or faxed to 740-826-6131. Please include the position title in the subject line of your correspondence. Muskingum University actively seeks out and welcomes administrators and staff who are committed to excellence in student learning, consider the engagement of diverse viewpoints in the University’s educational programs and activities, and are committed to full inclusivity at the University. Muskingum University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes applications from all individuals. Muskingum University does not discriminate in its employment or educational programs or activities. Please visit https://www.muskingum.edu/non-discrimination-statement to review the university’s official non-discrimination statement. Human Resources Human Resources Careers Benefits opener Wellness Financial Retirement Leave Campus Amenities Downloadable Forms Policies Staff Council Student Employment Contact Back to top Main menu About opener Admission & Aid opener Academics opener Campus Life opener Graduate & Adult Learning opener 260 Stadium Drive New Concord, Ohio 43762-1837 (740) 826-8211 facebook twitter instagram youtube Footer Right Accreditations & Affiliations Human Resources Consumer Information Net Price Calculator Non-Discrimination Statement Website Feedback Title IX Veterans Facebook Pixel"
    },
    "https://www.muskingum.edu/human-resources/system-mechanic-and-maintenance-supervisor": {
      "title": "System Mechanic and Maintenance Supervisor",
      "description": "System Mechanic and Maintenance Supervisor | Muskingum University Skip to main navigation main menu Search Tools Canvas Campus Directory Employee Navigator MuskieLink Microsoft 365 Main menu About opener Mission & Values Quick Facts Our Alumni History Map & Directions Office of the President Admission & Aid opener Apply Visit Financial Aid Request Info Pay Deposit Transfer Students International Admission Login Academics opener Majors & Minors Disability Resource Services Registrar Academic Affairs eCampus Books Campus Life opener Academic Services Living on Campus Get Involved Recreation Safety & Wellness Student Life Campus Map Impact Center Graduate & Adult Learning opener Adult Degree Completion Master of Business Administration Master of Arts in Education Master of Arts in Teaching Health Related Programs Master of Occupational Therapy Master of Organizational Leadership Doctor of Organizational Leadership Accelerated Bachelor of Science in Nursing Online RN to BSN Nursing Master of Science in Nursing: Leadership & Education Secondary Menu Alumni Giving News Events Arts Athletics Library Directory Campus Map Gear Shop A-Z tools search Human Resources Home Human Resources System Mechanic and Maintenance Supervisor System Mechanic and Maintenance Supervisor Muskingum University invites applications for a System Mechanic & Maintenance Supervisor.  This position ensures maintenance and repair of campus systems, such as HVAC, electrical, boiler, steam, plumbing, and other associated equipment systems, in a manner that minimizes the downtime of repairs and maximizes daily operation. Wage range between $40-50/hour, based on experience and certifications.  Muskingum offers a full benefits package, which includes a generous paid-time off package and immediate access to tuition remission or exchange for employees who are eligible.  More information about benefits is available at: https://www.muskingum.edu/human-resources/benefits . MAJOR RESPONSIBILITIES Suggest and implement changes in equipment for more efficient operation. Coordinate limited-scope construction projects. Supervise maintenance staff, including assessment and delegation of work assignments. Foster teamwork and coordination of effort among staff and continue collaboration between personnel assigned to maintenance and grounds. Provide professional development opportunities where appropriate. Comply with regulatory agency requirements (chemical hygiene, hazardous materials, OSHA, etc.) Perform staff evaluations. Maintain repair/supplies inventory. Order materials using the physical plant purchase order program, review invoices, and assign appropriate account numbers to invoices. Work within budget limitations. Maintain safe environment for staff and students. Develop and coordinate working relationships with vendors, suppliers, and contractors to maintain the campus. Conduct regularly building and HVAC quality assurance checks. Record reading from gauges and meters for pressure, temperature, water levels, etc. Conduct routine maintenance and any necessary repairs to heating, ventilation, air conditioning, refrigeration, pneumatic systems, steam systems, and boilers. Ability to use specialized tools to troubleshoot then diagnose faculty components for repair or replacement. Perform regular preventive maintenance, such as filter replacement, fluid changes, water treatment, lubrications, ect. Ability to utilize computers and handhelds to remotely monitor and adjust building environment conditions. Assist other trades; and division when needed. The above statements reflect the general duties and responsibilities necessary to describe the major functions of the position and should not be considered a complete description of the essential functions of the position.  This Job Description is not intended to be all inclusive.  The employee will be assigned by the immediate supervisor to perform other duties as needed or to perform other reasonably related duties, including special projects. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Ability to perform manual tasks requiring moderate strength. Ability to safely and correctly use machines and specialized tools for repair and maintenance. Working knowledge of building materials and their applications. Good communication and interpersonal skills. Good problem solving and diagnostic ability Ability to work in cramped spaces, inherently dirty locations, excessive heat, outdoors in a variety of weather and wet conditions. Available for after-hour emergencies as may occur from time to time. Must have and maintain a valid Ohio driver’s license and be insurable through the University’s carrier. HOW TO APPLY Applications must include a statement of interest and current resume.  If not provided, references may be requested.  Application materials should be sent by email to careers@muskingum.edu or faxed to 740-826-6131.  Please include the position title in the subject line of your correspondence.  This position will remain open until filled, with review of applications to begin immediately. Muskingum University actively seeks out and welcomes administrators and staff who are committed to excellence in student learning, consider the engagement of diverse viewpoints in the University’s educational programs and activities, and are committed to full inclusivity at the University.  Muskingum University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes applications from all individuals. Muskingum University does not discriminate in its employment or educational programs or activities.  Please visit https://www.muskingum.edu/non-discrimination-statement to review the university’s official non-discrimination statement. Human Resources Human Resources Careers Benefits opener Wellness Financial Retirement Leave Campus Amenities Downloadable Forms Policies Staff Council Student Employment Contact Back to top Main menu About opener Admission & Aid opener Academics opener Campus Life opener Graduate & Adult Learning opener 260 Stadium Drive New Concord, Ohio 43762-1837 (740) 826-8211 facebook twitter instagram youtube Footer Right Accreditations & Affiliations Human Resources Consumer Information Net Price Calculator Non-Discrimination Statement Website Feedback Title IX Veterans Facebook Pixel"
    },
    "https://www.muskingum.edu/human-resources/campus-amenities": {
      "title": "Campus Amenities",
      "description": "Campus Amenities | Muskingum University Skip to main navigation main menu Search Tools Canvas Campus Directory Employee Navigator MuskieLink Microsoft 365 Main menu About opener Mission & Values Quick Facts Our Alumni History Map & Directions Office of the President Admission & Aid opener Apply Visit Financial Aid Request Info Pay Deposit Transfer Students International Admission Login Academics opener Majors & Minors Disability Resource Services Registrar Academic Affairs eCampus Books Campus Life opener Academic Services Living on Campus Get Involved Recreation Safety & Wellness Student Life Campus Map Impact Center Graduate & Adult Learning opener Adult Degree Completion Master of Business Administration Master of Arts in Education Master of Arts in Teaching Health Related Programs Master of Occupational Therapy Master of Organizational Leadership Doctor of Organizational Leadership Accelerated Bachelor of Science in Nursing Online RN to BSN Nursing Master of Science in Nursing: Leadership & Education Secondary Menu Alumni Giving News Events Arts Athletics Library Directory Campus Map Gear Shop A-Z tools search Human Resources Home Human Resources Campus Amenities Campus Amenities Faculty and staff involvement makes our community stronger! The following activities and amenities promote learning and wellness, provide opportunities for engagement with students and colleagues, and strengthen the Muskie community. Identification Cards :  at the start of employment, faculty, administrators, and staff who are regularly scheduled to work more than 20 hours per week will be issued an ID card.  Free ID cards for the employee's immediate family may be requested from Campus Services by calling 740-826-8080. Campus employees have the right to inspect ID cards before granting access to the activities and amenities listed below. Campus Dining In addition to a variety of delicious meal options, eating in one of the campus dining facilities provides an excellent opportunity to engage with and support students. BAIT Shop :  located on the first floor of the Quad Center, the BAIT Shop is open to all faculty, staff, and their immediate family members for breakfast, lunch, and snacks during the academic year.  In addition to its own menu, the BAIT Shop proudly serves Starbucks coffee and pastries. Patton Dining Hall :  located on the first floor of Patton Hall, the D-Hall, as it is known to students, is open to all faculty, staff, and their immediate family members. Vending machines for soft drinks and snacks are located in several academic buildings. Cash, credit card, and Muskie Bucks are accepted at the BAIT Shop and Patton Dining Hall.  Starbucks gift cards may not be redeemed at the BAIT Shop. Muskie Bucks may be purchased through Campus Services* and will be loaded to the employee's ID card. *This location is not accessible; please call 740-826-8080 for service. Campus Events Athletic Events :  the cost of admission to most home athletic events is waived for employees, their spouses, and dependents. Cultural Events :  the University offers a rich blend of cultural events throughout the year, including concerts, plays, art exhibitions, and lectures.  The cost of admission to most events is waived for employees, their spouses, and dependents; however, a nominal admission fee may be required to attend certain events. Library All library services are available at no cost to all employees, and their immediate family members. Recreational Facilities Full-time employees, their spouses, and dependents may use campus recreation facilities free of charge and during the times designated by the Athletic Director.  Access times will be posted; however, before using any recreational facilities, the employee must complete and submit the Assumption of Risk, Waiver, and Release Form to the Human Resources Office. The employee is responsible for appropriate supervision of dependents at all times. Parking Eligible employees: all employees Effective date: upon hire Employee cost: $0 Employees are required to display a University-issued parking tag on the rearview mirror of their registered vehicle.  New employees may obtain their parking tag through the Human Resources Office.*  To replace a parking tag or update your vehicle information, please visit the University Police Department.* *These locations are not accessible; please call HR at 740-826-8119 or University Police at 740-826-8155 for service. Check Cashing Eligible employees: all employees Effective date: upon hire Employee cost: $0 Employees may cash personal checks of up to $25 by visiting the cashier, located in Montgomery Hall* 126. *This building is not accessible; please call 740-826-8111 for service. Notary Public Eligible employees: all employees Effective date: upon hire Employee cost: $0 Notary services are available by visiting the Business Office, located in Montgomery Hall* 125. *This building is not accessible; please call 740-826-8126 for service. Uniforms Eligible employees: University Police Officers and physical plant personnel Effective date: upon hire Employee cost: $0 The University provides uniforms, as needed, to University Police Officers and an annual clothing allowance to custodial, grounds, and maintenance personnel. This website is for informational purposes only and contains a summary of the financial benefits and programs available to eligible employees. The information on this webpage does not create any right to participate in or utilize any identified benefit.  Muskingum University may add to, change, or revoke any portion of its benefit program at any time and in its sole discretion. Human Resources Human Resources Careers Benefits opener Wellness Financial Retirement Leave Campus Amenities Downloadable Forms Policies Staff Council Student Employment Contact Back to top Main menu About opener Admission & Aid opener Academics opener Campus Life opener Graduate & Adult Learning opener 260 Stadium Drive New Concord, Ohio 43762-1837 (740) 826-8211 facebook twitter instagram youtube Footer Right Accreditations & Affiliations Human Resources Consumer Information Net Price Calculator Non-Discrimination Statement Website Feedback Title IX Veterans Facebook Pixel"
    }
